From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: McKack <4465550+McKack@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 02:25:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] airconv, d3d12: mesh and amplification shaders

DXIL mesh shaders become Metal mesh functions and amplification shaders Metal
object functions; D3D12 gets mesh pipelines from pipeline state streams,
ID3D12GraphicsCommandList3-6 and DispatchMesh, and reports mesh shader tier 1.

- Vertex and primitive outputs: the component stores of one row and vertex or
  primitive in a block are written as one Metal mesh field (rows laid out like
  vertex shader outputs, so pixel shaders link by name); rows written in parts
  go through a threadgroup copy. SV_CullPrimitive -> primitive_culled.
- The amplification shader's groupshared payload is copied to the object
  payload by all threads at DispatchMesh, then one thread sets the mesh grid.
- Raw/structured buffer addresses index dwords when 4-byte aligned: Metal's
  compiler crashes on byte-indexed addresses computed from a payload value.
- Mesh pipelines without a pixel shader get an empty fragment function.
- Root arguments and static samplers are bound to the object and mesh stages.
- Render passes (List4) map to render targets, clears and resolves; raytracing,
  meta commands and shading rate are no-ops (not reported).
- airconv -metal32.
